WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.520
Green hills.

2
00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:02.880
A stream.

3
00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:08.110
At golden noon, blue-black smoke
drifts up into sapphire skies.

4
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:13.470
And over it, again and again, a
promise: "I shall return again;

5
00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.680
I shall return" Streams
and mountain waters.

6
00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:20.010
Fiddles at village dances.

7
00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:23.580
Then the last word of the sonnet: pain.

8
00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:26.140
Fourteen lines of happy memories.

9
00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:29.260
So why does the last word say pain?

10
00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:31.810
In this mission, you'll
follow Claude McKay,

11
00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.310
who left Jamaica for the USA in 1912.

12
00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.540
You'll gather what he
remembers, sense by sense:

13
00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:40.830
sight, touch and sound.

14
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.520
And you'll count how often this
sonnet repeats its promise.

15
00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:48.350
Your mission: explain why
the last word is pain.
